msgid "Type: `Function`<br> Returns: `Object`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:168
msgid ""
"Prompter function which takes your [prompt objects](#-prompt-objects) and"
" returns an object with responses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:171
msgid "prompts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:173
msgid "Type: `Array|Object`<br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:175
msgid ""
"Array of [prompt objects](#-prompt-objects).  These are the questions the"
" user will be prompted. You can see the list of supported [prompt types "
"here](#-types)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:178
msgid ""
"Prompts can be submitted (<kbd>return</kbd>, <kbd>enter</kbd>) or "
"canceled (<kbd>esc</kbd>, <kbd>abort</kbd>, <kbd>ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>c</kbd>,"
" <kbd>ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>d</kbd>). No property is being defined on the "
"returned response object when a prompt is canceled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:180
msgid "options.onSubmit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:182 ../../source/prompts_readme.md:201
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Type: `Function`<br> Default: `() => {}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:185
msgid ""
"Callback that's invoked after each prompt submission. Its signature is "
"`(prompt, answer, answers)` where `prompt` is the current prompt object, "
"`answer` the user answer to the current question and `answers` the user "
"answers so far. Async functions are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:188
msgid ""
"Return `true` to quit the prompt chain and return all collected responses"
" so far, otherwise continue to iterate prompt objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:190 ../../source/prompts_readme.md:210
#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:273 ../../source/prompts_readme.md:386
#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:403
msgid "**Example:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:199
msgid "options.onCancel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:204
msgid ""
"Callback that's invoked when the user cancels/exits the prompt. Its "
"signature is `(prompt, answers)` where `prompt` is the current prompt "
"object and `answers` the user answers so far. Async functions are "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:207
msgid ""
"Return `true` to continue and prevent the prompt loop from aborting. On "
"cancel responses collected so far are returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:222
msgid "override"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:224 ../../source/prompts_readme.md:378
#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:398 ../../source/prompts_readme.md:416
msgid "Type: `Function`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:226
msgid ""
"Preanswer questions by passing an object with answers to "
"`prompts.override`. Powerful when combined with arguments of process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:229
msgid "**Example**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:257
msgid "inject(values)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:259
msgid "Type: `Function`<br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:261
msgid ""
"Programmatically inject responses. This enables you to prepare the "
"responses ahead of time. If any injected value is found the prompt is "
"immediately resolved with the injected value. This feature is intended "
"for testing only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:265
msgid "values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:267
msgid "Type: `Array`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:269
msgid ""
"Array with values to inject. Resolved values are removed from the "
"internal inject array. Each value can be an array of values in order to "
"provide answers for a question asked multiple times. If a value is an "
"instance of `Error` it will simulate the user cancelling/exiting the "
"prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:305
msgid "❯ Prompt Objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:307
msgid ""
"Prompts Objects are JavaScript objects that define the \"questions\" and "
"the [type of prompt](#-types). Almost all prompt objects have the "
"following properties:"
msgstr ""

