msgid ""
"Callback for when the prompt is rendered. The function receives "
"[kleur](https://github.com/lukeed/kleur) as its first argument and `this`"
" refers to the current prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md ../../source/prompts_readme.md:414
msgid "onState"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:418
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Callback for when the state of the current prompt changes. The function "
"signature is `(state)` where `state` is an object with a snapshot of the "
"current state. The state object has two properties `value` and `aborted`."
" E.g `{ value: 'This is ', aborted: false }`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:422
msgid "stdin and stdout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:424
msgid "Type: `Stream`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/prompts_readme.md:426
msgid ""
"By default, prompts uses `process.stdin` for receiving input and "
"`process.stdout` for writing output. If you need to use different "
"streams, for instance `process.stderr`, you can set these with the "
"`stdin` and `stdout` properties."
msgstr ""

